From 92e76e4bb012833b0eaad5c4cbb0be34795e2d94 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 15:19:39 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] feat(ui): Machines pane - browse and validate machine
 configurations

First slice of #287: a dockable, read-only Machines pane, opened and
closed from the ribbon's View door beside the properties pane. It lists
the shipped machine library plus the document's own mounted .mch file,
and shows the selected machine's validation (pass, or every refusal by
name) and its properties in collapsible groups.

App layer: machine::library (catalogue: builtins, scan_dir, enumerate;
per machine its kind, axes, rotaries, units, serving built-in posts and
a property sheet in the file's own units) and machine::validate
(validate_text -> named refusals: travel min < max, feeds/speeds above
0, M-word codes, live_tool all-or-none, units, required keys per kind;
malformed JSON is a refusal, never a panic). The pane reads no file
itself. No create/edit/save/assign yet; decisions and the open owner
question (user machine folder) in docs/decisions/287-machines-pane.md.

Refs #287

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
